('advanced-native-1044', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1044-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["They could navigate the app, but still needed support to judge the accounts’ sources."],"options":["They understood the sources but could not move beyond the app’s opening screen.","They had only watched the demonstration and had not tried the controls themselves.","They could navigate the app, but still needed support to judge the accounts’ sources.","They had already identified the first-hand account without using the source notes."]},"advanced-native-1044-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["They can tap and scroll, but comparing the source notes is a separate skill.","They have learned navigation without yet learning how to assess those sources.","Their remaining question concerns the evidence behind the accounts, not how to move the screen.","Moving through the screens does not tell them which account is first-hand."],"options":["They can tap and scroll, but comparing the source notes is a separate skill.","They have learned navigation without yet learning how to assess those sources.","Their remaining question concerns the evidence behind the accounts, not how to move the screen.","Moving through the screens does not tell them which account is first-hand."]},"advanced-native-1044-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["She can tap and scroll through the form, but still needs the difference between saving and confirming explained."],"options":["She has completed the separate confirmation step already.","She can tap and scroll through the form, but still needs the difference between saving and confirming explained.","She cannot reach the lower part of the form without someone moving the screen for her."]},"advanced-native-1044-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The person can already evaluate the reliability of everything displayed."],"options":["More information is needed to judge understanding of the content.","The person can perform some basic screen actions.","The person can already evaluate the reliability of everything displayed."]},"advanced-native-1044-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["They can tap and scroll; we should now explain the source notes and let them compare an example."],"options":["We should repeat only the navigation demonstration and leave the source question unanswered.","We can present their fluent navigation as proof that the first-hand account has been identified.","They can tap and scroll; we should now explain the source notes and let them compare an example."]},"advanced-native-1044-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The participant could tap and scroll, but the unlabelled symbols did not help him find the step-free entrance. We should add clear labels and ask him to try the route again.","Tapping and scrolling were not the problem; the map did not make the entrance clear. Let us test a labelled version rather than assume the participant needs more practice with the controls."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1045', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1045-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Practical ways to investigate a post’s authorship and timing."],"options":["Ready-made answers to the sample posts, without children practising the checks themselves.","Practical ways to investigate a post’s authorship and timing.","A list of headlines to repeat without checking their origin.","New devices in place of any practice with information."]},"advanced-native-1045-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It gives them a way to identify the author and check the date.","It equips children with checking habits through practice, rather than asking them to repeat the headline.","The exercises help them investigate where the information came from.","They practise questions that can guide their own judgement about the post."],"options":["It gives them a way to identify the author and check the date.","It equips children with checking habits through practice, rather than asking them to repeat the headline.","The exercises help them investigate where the information came from.","They practise questions that can guide their own judgement about the post."]},"advanced-native-1045-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The practice equips new guides with ways to clarify a question before answering."],"options":["The training focuses only on giving out microphones, without rehearsing a response.","The practice equips new guides with ways to clarify a question before answering.","The guides are given a fixed answer to recite for each possible question."]},"advanced-native-1045-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Children no longer need to judge new situations for themselves."],"options":["The teaching provides habits children can use.","Children no longer need to judge new situations for themselves.","Further practice may still be needed."]},"advanced-native-1045-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The session equips children with checking methods; we should describe their practice before claiming independent mastery."],"options":["Completing the guided task is enough to report that they now judge unfamiliar posts independently.","We should describe the author-and-date exercise as device training rather than information checking.","The session equips children with checking methods; we should describe their practice before claiming independent mastery."]},"advanced-native-1045-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The role-play can equip the volunteers with ways to ask about visitors’ preferences and listen to the answers. We should also practise when to seek a supervisor’s help.","We can equip young people with respectful questions rather than a list of assumptions about visitors. Further practice should include recognising when a request needs more support."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1046', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1046-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Some members could not see or discuss the changes when decisions were being made."],"options":["Some members could not see or discuss the changes when decisions were being made.","All members were discussing the latest plan together in the shared document.","The private thread was used only to repeat decisions everyone had already discussed.","The group had delayed any decisions until the remaining members arrived."]},"advanced-native-1046-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The process leaves them without timely access to the discussion.","The decisions are being made in a thread they cannot see.","The private discussion has become a barrier between students because the shared plan stays out of date.","They are left with an old version while others discuss the new arrangements elsewhere."],"options":["The process leaves them without timely access to the discussion.","The decisions are being made in a thread they cannot see.","The private discussion has become a barrier between students because the shared plan stays out of date.","They are left with an old version while others discuss the new arrangements elsewhere."]},"advanced-native-1046-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The shared screen is a barrier between students because it prevents them from seeing each other’s work."],"options":["The change allows questions about the drafts during the activity.","The shared viewing gives the students a way to discuss one another’s drafts.","The shared screen is a barrier between students because it prevents them from seeing each other’s work."]},"advanced-native-1046-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The students must be unwilling to cooperate with each other."],"options":["A particular factor is hindering their connection.","The students must be unwilling to cooperate with each other.","The context should identify what exchange is obstructed."]},"advanced-native-1046-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The restricted thread is a barrier between students; we should invite everyone into the discussion before judging their interest."],"options":["Their silence shows that the latest changes have already been discussed with them.","We should keep the changes in the same private thread and ask the others to comment on the old plan.","The restricted thread is a barrier between students; we should invite everyone into the discussion before judging their interest."]},"advanced-native-1046-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The rapid use of technical terms has become a barrier between students in this pair. Could each describe an observation first, before they check the terms together?","We can reduce a barrier between learners by giving both a turn to explain what they noticed. The quieter student needs an opening to contribute, not an assumption that there is nothing to say."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1047', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1047-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Familiar places led the group to ask historical questions and check dates."],"options":["The group used the photographs only as decoration and did not discuss them.","The guide gave dates before anyone recognised the streets or asked a question.","Recognising the streets replaced any further investigation of the market.","Familiar places led the group to ask historical questions and check dates."]},"advanced-native-1047-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["They could begin with something familiar before checking the dates and reasons.","The photographs encouraged investigation rather than just recognition.","The streets they recognised gave them a starting point for historical questions.","The images became a bridge to learning by connecting familiar places with questions about change."],"options":["They could begin with something familiar before checking the dates and reasons.","The photographs encouraged investigation rather than just recognition.","The streets they recognised gave them a starting point for historical questions.","The images became a bridge to learning by connecting familiar places with questions about change."]},"advanced-native-1047-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The measuring activity provided a bridge to learning about fractions, with further examples still to try."],"options":["The activity was unrelated to the fraction diagram the students discussed afterwards.","The teacher stopped all work on fractions before students connected the amounts.","The measuring activity provided a bridge to learning about fractions, with further examples still to try."]},"advanced-native-1047-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Providing the aid guarantees independent mastery."],"options":["Providing the aid guarantees independent mastery.","The connection it creates can be explained.","An aid helps people approach new understanding."]},"advanced-native-1047-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The photographs are a bridge to learning; let us use their questions to guide the date check rather than stop at recognition."],"options":["The photographs are a bridge to learning; let us use their questions to guide the date check rather than stop at recognition.","We should treat recognition of the street as a completed explanation of why the market changed.","We should ask them to identify the familiar streets again instead of following up the questions they raised."]},"advanced-native-1047-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The captioned stories can be a bridge to learning local sign language. They offer a starting point, while guided practice will help us begin using it respectfully.","Let us use the short stories as a bridge to learning, then join the introductory session to practise with a teacher. Watching the films is an invitation to begin, not a claim that we can already sign."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1048', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1048-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Flexible preparation at home and a shared discussion, with a meeting time still needed."],"options":["Members discuss the reading separately with the organiser, without a shared group meeting.","Notes read only during Saturday’s meeting, with no home preparation.","Flexible preparation at home and a shared discussion, with a meeting time still needed.","A fully independent course with no shared discussion."]},"advanced-native-1048-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["They feel they have the best of both worlds: flexible reading and a shared exchange of views.","The home notes preserve flexibility while Saturday gives them a chance to question one another.","The design combines individual preparation with conversation rather than making them choose only one.","They can prepare at their own time and still discuss their interpretations together."],"options":["They feel they have the best of both worlds: flexible reading and a shared exchange of views.","The home notes preserve flexibility while Saturday gives them a chance to question one another.","The design combines individual preparation with conversation rather than making them choose only one.","They can prepare at their own time and still discuss their interpretations together."]},"advanced-native-1048-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The partnership offers the best of both worlds: personal bookselling advice and access to borrowed copies, within the session’s capacity."],"options":["The library copies replace any opportunity to talk with the bookseller.","The partnership offers the best of both worlds: personal bookselling advice and access to borrowed copies, within the session’s capacity.","The arrangement turns the free discussion into a buyers-only event."]},"advanced-native-1048-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The arrangement has no limitations or trade-offs."],"options":["The favourable judgement