('advanced-native-1049', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1049-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["It shared memories alongside evidence and openly noted disagreements."],"options":["It presented every disagreement as settled before listeners heard the series.","It shared memories alongside evidence and openly noted disagreements.","It used the most dramatic memory as the final account whenever dates differed.","It removed the residents’ voices and broadcast only the photograph dates."]},"advanced-native-1049-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It connected residents’ recollections with records and made uncertainty visible.","It kept history alive through people’s memories while still showing where the evidence differed.","Listeners could hear experiences from the past without being told that every detail was certain.","The series offered engaging accounts and a clear distinction between memory and confirmed detail."],"options":["It connected residents’ recollections with records and made uncertainty visible.","It kept history alive through people’s memories while still showing where the evidence differed.","Listeners could hear experiences from the past without being told that every detail was certain.","The series offered engaging accounts and a clear distinction between memory and confirmed detail."]},"advanced-native-1049-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The project helps keep history alive while leaving uncertain dates open for checking."],"options":["The project helps keep history alive while leaving uncertain dates open for checking.","The project treats all the years recalled by alumni as already confirmed.","The photographs are displayed without any invitation to connect them with memories or places."]},"advanced-native-1049-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["A memorable retelling is therefore historically accurate."],"options":["People continue engaging with the past.","A memorable retelling is therefore historically accurate.","Evidence can still be checked alongside personal memories."]},"advanced-native-1049-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We can keep history alive through the recorded memories without presenting invented dialogue as evidence."],"options":["We can keep history alive through the recorded memories without presenting invented dialogue as evidence.","We should replace the uncertain account with a more detailed version even though no source supports the details.","We can label the new dialogue as a resident’s memory because it suits the programme’s theme."]},"advanced-native-1049-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["A monthly question could help keep history alive after the exhibition ends. We can link it to checked sources and invite additions, clearly marking contributions that still need verification.","Let us keep history alive through a continuing enquiry rather than a single visit. Readers can follow the sources and send what they remember, while unverified details remain labelled as such."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
